ge-8 columns"><p>You have exceeded the software activation limits for your subscription.</p></div>     <div class="large-4 columns right"><p><a href=""></a></p></div>      <p><img src="http://www.webroot.com/shared/images/webroot-logo-green.png" alt="Webroot Logo" /></p>      <h1>Important Service Notification</h1>         <p>Dear Webroot Customer:</p>         <p>Unfortunately, there is an issue with the keycode for your current Webroot product. This occurs when the product is installed on more devices than your subscription permits.  For reference, your product keycode is SAE6ZBNGABBE2C88BB93 and is valid for 3 Devices</p><p><strong>Due to activation limits, you will need to purchase an additional license or add devices to your current license for your subscription to remain active. If you do not take action, your subscription will be deactivated in 7 days.</strong></p>         <p class="center"><a href="https://www.webroot.com/us/en/cart/device_enforcement/?key=92ACD39D-7E2A-4493-A499-93FB7B68B0F4"><img src="http://www.webroot.com/shared/images/device-enforcement-upgrade-subscription-button.png" /></a></p>         <p>Please call our Customer Service Department at <strong>1-866-612-4268</strong> Monday through Friday 7am-7:30pm MT, or Saturdays & Sundays 7am-6pm MT to purchase an additional license or add devices to your license.</p>         <p>If you are not sure why this issue occurred and want to view and manage your installations, <a href="https://my.webrootanywhere.com/default.asp?action=login">click here</a> to access your Management Console.  Once logged in, you can view the different devices using your subscription, and deactivate devices as needed by clicking on PC Security and deactivating the corresponding device.  If SecureAnywhere is still installed on a device when you deactivate it, SecureAnywhere will uninstall itself from the device automatically. </p>         <p>Next to security, integrity is our priority.  Please help us make Webroot a better product for everyone.</p>         <p>We look forward to hearing from you soon.</p>         <p><img src="http://www.webroot.com/shared/images/device-enforcement-webroot-crew.png" alt="Webroot Crew" /></p>     </div> </div> </body> ',1,'2015-05-27T16:07:55.877');
